  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lead-paragraph">I like turning ideas into dependable, working software. Sometimes that means a distributed backend system handling millions of transactions. Sometimes it means an Android app that saves someone a few taps.</p>
    <p>I’m a Staff Software Engineer at PayPal in Bengaluru, where I focus on payments infrastructure and core backend systems. Over the past decade, my work has focused on distributed architectures, transactional resilience, APIs, and data pipelines.</p>
    <p>Before PayPal, I built software at AppZen, Clairvoyant, and Persistent Systems. That background across big data, financial AI audit, and enterprise systems shaped how I approach engineering: understand the moving parts deeply, design for clarity and failure modes, and build software that stays reliable over time.</p>
    <h2>Building small, useful tools</h2>
    <p>Outside of large backend platforms, I enjoy crafting <a href="/work/">independent apps and utilities</a>. <a href="/work/clean-my-links/">Clean My Links</a> removes tracking parameters from URLs before sharing. <a href="/work/minku-learns/">Minku Learns</a> offers an offline learning companion for early learners. <a href="/work/unknown-messenger/">Unknown Messenger</a> simplifies one-off WhatsApp conversations without saving temporary contacts.</p>
    <p>I’m also interested in practical applications of AI in software engineering workflows—such as <a href="/work/autolld/">AutoLLD</a>, which transforms codebases into clear Low-Level Design documents.</p>
    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>If you'd like to discuss distributed systems, software engineering, side projects, or share feedback on any of my apps, feel free to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">reach out via email</a> or connect on <a href="{{ site.linkedin }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
